    "narrative": "Ghost Ride the WHIP enters today\u2019s slate with a high-ceiling lineup led by **Vinnie Pasquantino** and **Trevor Story**, who command our top efficiency scores at 76.21 and 73.82, respectively. **Vinnie Pasquantino** benefits from a massive 14% platoon edge against Zac Gallen, while **Trevor Story** capitalizes on favorable wind conditions and a soft matchup against Ryan Johnson. **Mickey Moniak** (68.53) and **Corbin Carroll** (67.53) provide the critical speed-power dynamic we prioritize; **Mickey Moniak** is positioned for a breakout performance thanks to a 14% dynamic platoon advantage, and **Corbin Carroll** remains an essential start despite the slight penalty for facing Daniel Lynch IV. **James Wood** rounds out the elite tier at 66.45, buoyed by a stellar 0.419 xwOBA and the prime #1 spot in the order, even against a tough veteran like Walker Buehler.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench involved **Cole Young**, who posted a respectable 53.41 but ultimately fell short due to his projected lower-order placement and the crowded field of higher-efficiency options like **Travis Bazzana** and **Max Muncy**. While **Travis Bazzana** carries a solid 57.55, his value is bolstered by a significant 16% park factor boost, which outpaces the situational utility of our bench depth. We are monitoring the lineup status for all starters, specifically noting that **Gabriel Moreno** and **Jose Caballero** could see their efficiency scores shift if their assumed batting orders fluctuate upon the official release. While no major weather alerts threaten the board, managers should keep a close eye on the performance of **Josh Naylor** (62.78) against Cody Bradford, as his matchup relies heavily on his ability to exploit the SP\u2019s 5.27 xERA despite the minor park penalty.",
